{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (94.12%) to rattlesnake Crotalicidin. K: 38%; V: 12%, F: 18%. GRAVY: -0.48; M Wt: 4172.316; M formula: C205H341N53O37S1, mol ex coeff: 0. Activity: active against E. coli TOP10 or clinical strain (MIC 0.47 uM), S. aureus ATCC6538 or clinical strain (MIC 1.91 uM), P. aeruginosa or clinical strain (MIC 0.95 uM), S. saprophyticus ATCC BAA-750 (MIC 0.95 uM), S. typhymurium ATCC 14028 (MIC 1.91 uM), and E. casseliflavus ATCC 700327 (MIC 0.95 uM). parasites: Aquiluscidin inhibited B. ovata (IC50 14.48 uM) and B. bovis (IC50 20.7 uM). Activity is serum-sensitive:parasites ( Hernández-Arvizu et al., 2024). In vitro Toxicity: rat RBC: less than 3% hemolysis at 50 uM (incubated 30 min). HEK293 cells (IC50 ~35 uM). Structure: predicted to be amphipathic helix. Updated 6/2024", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "2076", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Microorganisms 2023; 11: 2778. https://doi.org/10.3390/microorganisms11112778. Publisher", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03818", "source_id": "AP03818", "source_numeric_id": "03818", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03818", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Aquiluscidin, a Cathelicidin from Crotalus aquilus, and the Vcn-23 Derivative Peptide, Have Anti-Microbial Activity against Gram-Negative and Gram-Positive Bacteria", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (67.65%) to rattlesnake Crotalicidin. K: 43%; V=F: 13%. GRAVY: -0.44; M Wt: 2849.707; M formula: C139H242N36O25S1, mol ex coeff: 0. Activity: active against E. coli TOP10 or clinical strain (MIC 0.70 uM), S. aureus ATCC6538 or clinical strain (MIC 1.40 uM), P. aeruginosa or clinical strain (MIC 1.40 uM), S. saprophyticus ATCC BAA-750 (MIC 0.70 uM), S. typhymurium ATCC 14028 (MIC 0.70 uM), and E. casseliflavus ATCC 700327 (MIC 0.70 uM). In vitro Toxicity: rat RBC: less than 2% hemolysis at 50 uM. HEK293 cells (IC50 ~60 uM). Structure: predicted to be amphipathic helix. Upated 6/2024", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "2076", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Microorganisms 2023; 11: 2778. https://doi.org/10.3390/microorganisms11112778. Publisher", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03819", "source_id": "AP03819", "source_numeric_id": "03819", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03819", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Aquiluscidin, a Cathelicidin from Crotalus aquilus, and the Vcn-23 Derivative Peptide, Have Anti-Microbial Activity against Gram-Negative and Gram-Positive Bacteria", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
